# Binaries
#
# `go build ./...` drops a binary named after each main package in the
# working directory. examples/receipt is the one that exists today.
#
# Unanchored on purpose: the binary lands in examples/receipt/, not at the
# repository root, and a leading slash here matched neither it nor anything
# else. It reached git six times before that was noticed.
receipt
*.exe
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib
/bin/
/dist/

# Where the Makefile puts binaries it builds on purpose, so that nothing lands
# beside its source (see the note above).
/.bin/

# Test and coverage output
*.test
*.out
coverage.*
/eval/report/*.local.*

# Fuzzing corpus additions found by the fuzzer
testdata/fuzz/

# Go workspace — local to each contributor
go.work
go.work.sum

# Editors
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*~
.DS_Store

# Environment
.env
.env.*
